text:
olivia: Hey team — kickstarting a POC with Horizon Bank. They want a week-long pilot to validate: streaming SDK (Node + Java), tool/function calls back to their webhook, and strict structured JSON output for downstream systems. Also they need to host in their VPC (onprem/private) and we have an internal security questionnaire to complete. Can we confirm what the minimal config is and any blockers?

raj: Gonna run through the checklist. Quick Q: do they need server-initiated callbacks (webhook) during the stream or only function calls embedded in responses?

olivia: They want tool calls during the stream so the model can ask for data, and webhook callbacks for long-running ops. Latency target is <300ms p95 for short messages.

kai: For streaming + funcalls we support SSE/ws with structured func payloads. If onprem VPC, we need to deploy Redwood Private agent in their network — that requires an outbound control-plane egress to our controller (or an airgap package). Any KMS/HSM constraints?

olivia: They insist on customer-managed KMS (AWS KMS) and SOC2 + ISO27001. Also want logs forwarded to their SIEM.

maria: Pricing side — Horizon asked if reserved capacity is required for predictable latency for the pilot or if burst/dedicated short-term is possible. What's the recommendation?

raj: For a week-long POC, we can do a short-term Dedicated pool (reserved hourly) if they want predictable p95. Otherwise hosted with pinning to a performance model might be OK but less deterministic. I'll draft a pricing estimate.

devon: Security questionnaire notes: for Private we can offer customer KMS integration, audit logs, and VPC peering. We need to surface: data-at-rest encryption (BYOK), no model weights uploaded by customer, access control (OIDC/SAML). I'll attach standard answers.

olivia: Can you paste the minimal network requirements and the SDK sample that shows a streaming funcall with structured output? I'll include in the RFP.

kai: Pasting a small Node example (streaming + funcall JSON schema):
```js
const stream = client.stream({model: 'redwood-1-large', stream: true});
stream.on('data', chunk => {
  // chunk: {type: 'response'|'tool_call'|'end', payload: {...}}
  if (chunk.type === 'tool_call') {
    // call customer's webhook
    fetch('https://horizon.example.com/hooks', {method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(chunk.payload)})
  }
});
```
Network: outbound HTTPS to control.redwood.com:443 for control plane; inbound only for customer webhook endpoints (we call out). For Private onprem, we need an egress to our artifact service unless they take the airgap build.

raj: Note: structured output can be enforced by a schema binder. We should run an eval against their sample prompts to ensure no schema drift. Recommend enabling strict JSON mode in the SDK.

olivia: Great. Any known blockers for SOC2 customers trying to run a week POC in Private?

devon: Timeline: security review + SOC2 artifacts can be answered in 2 business days for the questionnaire. Onprem deploy takes ~3-5 business days for our infra/packaging + their infra team scheduling. KMS key setup and RBAC config usually 1 day if they have AWS admin ready.

maria: For pricing: I'll offer a trial credit + an ops fee for Private provisioning. I'll share draft numbers tomorrow.

olivia: Horizon also asked about token-based throttling and prefix caching to reduce cost. Any docs I can share?

kai: Send them the Optimize playbook link (redwood.com/docs/optimize) and mention prefix/KV caching toggles in the config. Also we can enable auto-batching heuristics for the Dedicated pool.

sre-bot: deploy-bot: New Private deployment request queued (#REQ-4582). ETA initial staging infra: 72 hours.

raj: Next steps: I'll produce a short POC runbook (steps + expected artifacts) and a sample Postman / SDK snippet for their infra team. Olivia — can you confirm the business contact and infra contact?

olivia: Confirmed: horizon-poc@horizon.com (biz), infra lead is j.singh@horizon.com. I'll DM the NDA and security questionnaire. Thanks all :thumbsup:
